### Publishing to Docker Hub

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` builds a `linux/amd64` + `linux/arm64` image {% if docker_builder == 'cloud' %}on Docker Build Cloud (`{{ build_cloud_builder }}`){% else %}on the GitHub runner (QEMU){% endif %} and pushes it to `{{ dockerhub_image }}`:

| Trigger | Tags |
| --- | --- |
| push to `main` | `latest`, `sha-<short sha>` |
| tag `v1.2.3` | `1.2.3`, `1.2` |
| pull request | build only, no push |

Add these repository secrets (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions):

- `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME`: your Docker Hub username
- `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN`: a Docker Hub access token with Read & Write scope
{%- if docker_builder == 'cloud' %}

The token's account must have access to the Build Cloud builder `{{ build_cloud_builder }}`. Pull requests from forks get no secrets, so their build fails. That's expected.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

## Dependencies

No versions are hardcoded. `scripts/deps.py` adds packages by name, so `uv` resolves the latest releases and locks them in `uv.lock`.

- `make upgrade` bumps every package to its latest release.
- `make deps` re-runs the resolution from scratch.
